      "message": "This still appears unfixed in patchset 37: `IS_FLOW_ENABLED()` only checks that `hw_if_index !\u003d ~0`, so an enable callback that records a different interface passes this postcondition. A later disable would then dispatch through the wrong interface and could leave the original hardware rule installed. Could we also require `f-\u003edriver_data.hw_if_index \u003d\u003d hw_if_index` here?",
      "parentUuid": "47be15a4_687fe100",
      "revId": "86e15df9d009e735fb5024e8d61d706af56069e3",
      "serverId": "6d2eb258-4fe2-443e-8a38-ca81da23d4c2"
    },
